</span></div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S5.T4.8" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><sup id="S5.T4.8.1" class="ltx_sup"><math id="S5.T4.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dagger" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="0.800em">†</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dagger</annotation></semantics></math></sup><span id="S5.T4.8.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">BFCL v4 excluding web-search category.
<br class="ltx_break"><sup id="S5.T4.8.2.1" class="ltx_sup"><math id="S5.T4.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ddagger" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>‡</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddagger</annotation></semantics></math></sup>SciCode problem-level pass @1 (reported here) requires every subtask to be solved, so absolute scores are single-digit and relative <math id="S5.T4.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>s are sensitive to small gaps. Absolute point gaps: <math id="S5.T4.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\text{GKA-GDN}}=+3.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext>GKA-GDN</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3.9</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\text{GKA-GDN}}=+3.9</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.T4.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\text{source}}=-4.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext>source</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4.2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\text{source}}=-4.2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.T4.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\text{SFT}}=+2.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2.3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\text{SFT}}=+2.3</annotation></semantics></math>. <a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 SciCode Problem vs. Subtask Accuracy ‣ Appendix D Additional Reasoning Results ‣ Priming: Hybrid State Space Models From Pre-trained Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> reports the subtask-level pass @1; rankings are preserved.<span id="S5.T4.8.2.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8B Models.</span> In <a href="#S5.T4" title="In 5.2 Primed Reasoning Model Results ‣ 5 Priming: Main Results ‣ Priming: Hybrid State Space Models From Pre-trained Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> we report the reasoning performance of our Primed Hybrid Reasoner models at 8B scale. We make the following observations.</p>
<ul id="S5.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Primed Hybrid models deliver 1.8-2.3<math id="S5.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> higher decode throughput on long-reasoning tasks while being competitive with the Transformer baseline on reasoning benchmarks.</span> As in the IT setting (<a href="#S5.SS1.SSS1" title="5.1.1 Long-context Evaluation ‣ 5.1 Primed Instruct Model Results ‣ 5 Priming: Main Results ‣ Priming: Hybrid State Space Models From Pre-trained Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1.1</span></a>), the roughly 50% smaller KV cache of our Primed Hybrids translates to a 1.8-2.3<math id="S5.I6.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> decode speedup over the Transformer. Against the Qwen3-8B [Reasoner-SFT] baseline, which is fine-tuned on the same reasoning SFT data with the same hyperparameters and thus isolates the architectural difference, the GKA-based Reasoner trails by only <math id="S5.I6.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>1% (relative) in aggregate and the GDN-based Reasoner by <math id="S5.I6.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>4.0% (relative).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The GKA-based Reasoner matches or outperforms the GDN-based Reasoner uniformly across all tasks.</span> This is in contrast to the IT setting, where the two Hybrids performed on par at both long and short context (<a href="#S5.T2" title="In 5.1.2 Short-context Evaluation ‣ 5.1 Primed Instruct Model Results ‣ 5 Priming: Main Results ‣ Priming: Hybrid State Space Models From Pre-trained Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tables</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#S5.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 5.1.1 Long-context Evaluation ‣ 5.1 Primed Instruct Model Results ‣ 5 Priming: Main Results ‣ Priming: Hybrid State Space Models From Pre-trained Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). Reasoning tasks are substantially more challenging: unlike IT workloads, which feature long context inputs but short responses, reasoning tasks require the model to generate long chains of thought before answering. GKA’s more expressive state update better preserves intermediate computations across these extended thinking traces, which translates directly into higher accuracy on reasoning benchmarks.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I6.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Our reasoning recipe improves both the Transformer and the Primed Hybrids over the off-the-shelf Qwen3-8B.</span> The Qwen3-8B [Reasoner-SFT] baseline and both Primed Hybrid Reasoners outperform the off-the-shelf Qwen3-8B in aggregate, confirming the efficacy of our reasoning training recipe (<a href="#S10.SS3" title="10.3 Long-Context Reasoning ‣ 10 Training Recipes ‣ Priming: Hybrid State Space Models From Pre-trained Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.3</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T5" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="S5.T5.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Reasoning evaluation at 32B scale.<span id="S5.T5.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Performance of our Primed Hybrid Reasoner model (GKA) against the Qwen3-32B off-the-shelf source Transformer and the Qwen3-32B [Reasoner-SFT] baseline fine-tuned with the same reasoning recipe. All models are evaluated at 64K generation length with thinking mode on. The <span id="S5.T5.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Avg.</span> column reports the aggregate performance across all eight benchmarks. <math id="S5.T5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\text{source}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext>source</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\text{source}}</annotation></semantics></math>% and <math id="S5.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\text{SFT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\text{SFT}}</annotation></semantics></math>% report the relative gap (per task) of GKA-Primed-HQwen3-Reasoner against the Qwen3-32B and Qwen3-32B [Reasoner-SFT] baselines respectively.</span></span></figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
