<section id="S11.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">8B models.</h5>

<div id="S11.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S11.T14" title="In 8B models. ‣ 11.1 Decode Throughput ‣ 11 Inference and Deployment ‣ Priming: Hybrid State Space Models From Pre-trained Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> reports the same benchmark at 8B scale. All three pure-SSM-based Primed Hybrid types, GKA, GDN, and Mamba2, show the pattern predicted by Equation <a href="#S11.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ A model of decode throughput. ‣ 11 Inference and Deployment ‣ Priming: Hybrid State Space Models From Pre-trained Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>: speedups grow monotonically with context length, from <math id="S11.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.86" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.86</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.86</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S11.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.95\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.95</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.95\times</annotation></semantics></math> at 16K to <math id="S11.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.26" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.26</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.26</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S11.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.33\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.33</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.33\times</annotation></semantics></math> at 128K. GKA-Primed-HQwen3 is approximately <math id="S11.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S11.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\%</annotation></semantics></math> slower than GDN- and Mamba2-based Hybrids across all context lengths, reflecting the additional compute of the Chebyshev solve within each GKA layer; reducing <span id="S11.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">num_iter</span> narrows this gap (<a href="#S8.SS2" title="8.2 Variable Test-time Compute with GKA ‣ 8 Gated KalmaNet: A Fading Memory SSM Layer with Variable Test-time Compute ‣ Priming: Hybrid State Space Models From Pre-trained Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S11.T14" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S11.T14.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 14</span>: </span><span id="S11.T14.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Measured decode throughput (tokens/s) for our 8B Primed Hybrid models on <math id="S11.T14.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\times</annotation></semantics></math> H200 (TP=8) under KV-cache saturation. Speedup over the Qwen3-8B Transformer baseline shown in parentheses.
</span></figcaption>
